FORBIDDEN ARCHIVE -- WARNING CONCERNING SHUKAKU, THE ONE-TAIL
Kazekage Office seal required for access. Do NOT copy.

Shukaku, the One-Tailed Tanuki, is the tailed beast historically sealed
within Sunagakure's jinchuriki. This document exists to warn, not to instruct.

Known dangers:
- The beast whispers to its host during sleep. A jinchuriki who loses
  consciousness risks the seal weakening and the sand-form manifesting
  uncontrolled. Insomnia has afflicted every recorded host.
- Shukaku commands wind and sand at overwhelming scale and can force a partial
  transformation the host cannot easily reverse.
- Any deliberate summoning or forced manifestation of the beast within village
  walls is a forbidden act punishable under the highest edict.

The current jinchuriki, the Fifth Kazekage Lord Gaara, has achieved a measure
of control unknown to prior hosts. Nonetheless, no shinobi is to provoke,
research, or attempt extraction of the beast. Abduction of the jinchuriki is
treated as an act of war against the village. Filed under permanent seal.
